 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Matching.lean exposes only `isMatching_def`, `isMatching_congr`, `isMatching_effectiveAmplitude` for `IsMatching`; the repo's analogous predicate does carry it \u2014 `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/TMD/PowerCorrections.lean:116` `lemma ApproximatesToOrder.mono ... (hmn : m \u2264 n) : ApproximatesToOrder W Wapp m`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Quarkonium/NRQCD/Matching.lean",
   "fix": "Add `IsMatching.mono : P.IsMatching n F M c \u2192 m \u2264 n \u2192 P.IsMatching m F M c`; the difference of the two effective amplitudes is `\u2211_{m < totalDegree o \u2264 n} c o * M a o * \u03b5 ^ totalDegree o`, each term `O(\u03b5 ^ (m+1))` on `\ud835\udcdd[>] 0`.",
   "issue": "`IsMatching` has no lemma relating `IsMatching n` to `IsMatching m` for `m \u2264 n`, so the order parameter of the main definition is uncharacterized and assignments matching to different orders cannot be compared.",
   "line": 157
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Line 133 `effectiveAmplitude_congr (hM : Set.EqOn M M' (P.truncation n)) (hc : ...)`; line 173 instantiates it as `P.effectiveAmplitude_congr (Set.eqOn_refl _ _) h`, leaving the `M` side unreachable through `IsMatching`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Quarkonium/NRQCD/Matching.lean",
   "fix": "Generalize `isMatching_congr` to also take `hM : \u2200 a, Set.EqOn (M a) (M' a) (P.truncation n)` and conclude `P.IsMatching n F M c \u2194 P.IsMatching n F M' c'`.",
   "issue": "`isMatching_congr` only takes `hc`, dropping the matrix-element congruence that `effectiveAmplitude_congr` supplies, so `IsMatching` cannot be transferred along matrix elements that agree on the truncation.",
   "line": 170
  }
 ],
